-- title:
--   Pseudo-Eisenstein inner product over a determinant slab
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, with adele ring $\mathbb{A}$ and $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ carrying its Borel $\sigma$-algebra and Haar measure `adelicGLHaar`. Let $0<d_1<d_2$ be reals and let $\Phi\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ be contained in the determinant slab $\{g:\|\det g\|\in[d_1,d_2]\}$, where $\|\cdot\|$ is the idele norm given by the module of the translation action on $\mathbb{A}$, and be a fundamental domain, in Mathlib's sense, for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ acting on the Haar measure restricted to that slab. The data $\Phi$, the level subgroups $N\mapsto$ `levelOne`, the Hecke generators $v\mapsto$ `heckeGen` and the adelic box assemble into a `CarrierPins` record whose central subgroup $Z$ is all of $(\mathbb{A})^\times$, whose measure is `adelicGLHaar` and whose domain is $\Phi$; let $\xi:Z\to\mathbb{C}^\times$ be a character. Let $\varphi,\psi:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})\to\mathbb{C}$ both be slab profiles for $\xi$, i.e. measurable, invariant under left translation by all $n(x)=\begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, $x\in\mathbb{A}$, and by all $F$-rational matrices with vanishing $(1,0)$ entry, satisfying $\varphi(z g)=\xi(z)\varphi(g)$ for central scalars $z\in Z$, bounded on every slab $\{\|\det g\|\in[d_1,d_2]\}$ with $d_1>0$, and vanishing outside a band $a\le \mathrm{adelicHeight}(g)\le b$ with $a>0$. Writing $\theta_\varphi(g)=\varphi(g)+\sum_{\beta\in F}\varphi(w\,n(\beta)g)$ for the pseudo-Eisenstein series, $w$ being the image of the $\mathrm{GL}_2$ Weyl element, the assertion is $$\int_\Phi \theta_\varphi(g)\,\overline{\theta_\psi(g)}\,d\mu(g)=\int_{\{q:\|\det q^{\mathrm{out}}\|\in[d_1,d_2]\}}\varphi(q^{\mathrm{out}})\,\overline{\Big(\psi(q^{\mathrm{out}})+\mathrm{vol}(\mathcal{B})^{-1}\,M\psi(q^{\mathrm{out}})\Big)}\,dq,$$ where the right-hand integral is over the quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ by the orbit relation of the subgroup generated by the rational torus and the adelic unipotent group, $q^{\mathrm{out}}$ denotes a chosen representative of the class $q$, $dq$ is `rationalTorusUnipotentQuotientMeasure`, the pushforward of `adelicGLHaar` weighted by the density attached to `rationalTorusUnipotentHaar`, $M\psi(g)=\int_{\mathbb{A}}\psi(w^{-1}n(x)g)\,dx$ is taken against the unconditioned adelic additive Haar measure, and $\mathrm{vol}(\mathcal{B})$ is the real volume of the adelic box (the lattice fundamental domain at the infinite places times the integral finite adeles) for that same measure.
--
--   This is the inner-product formula for two pseudo-Eisenstein series attached to slab profiles: the pairing over a fundamental domain in the determinant slab is rewritten as a pairing on the rational-torus–unipotent quotient, with the constant term of the second series appearing as $\psi$ plus the normalised Weyl intertwining integral of $\psi$. It feeds the further reduction of this pairing to a sum of integrals over the maximal compact subgroup.
